  _globals['_INSPECTIONSERVICE'].methods_by_name['MCPInspect']._serialized_options = b'\222A\343\021\n\016MCP Inspection\022!Inspect MCP JSON-RPC 2.0 Messages\032\324\007Inspects Model Context Protocol (MCP) messages for security, safety, and privacy violations. Automatically detects message type (request/response/notification) from JSON-RPC structure.\n\n**Message Type Detection:**\n- Request: has \'method\' + \'id\' (client\342\206\222server, expects response)\n- Response: has \'result\'/\'error\' + \'id\' (server\342\206\222client)\n- Notification: has \'method\', no \'id\' (one-way, no response)\n\n**Use Cases:**\n- Inspect tool calls before execution (e.g., database queries, file access)\n- Validate resource access requests (e.g., file URIs, network resources)\n- Scan prompt template arguments for injection attacks\n- Check responses for data leakage (PII, credentials, secrets)\n\n**Authentication & Configuration:**\n- API key must be provided in X-Cisco-AI-Defense-API-Key header\n- MCP context (connection_id, server_id, tenant_id) extracted from API key\n- Inspection rules and policies configured server-side per tenant\n- No need to specify metadata or config in request body*\nmcpInspectJ\307\001\n\003200\022\277\001\n\274\001Inspection completed successfully. Returns MCP JSON-RPC 2.0 response with inspection results in the \'result\' field. Check result.is_safe to determine if the MCP message is safe to process.J\376\001\n\003400\022\366\001\n\363\001Bad Request - Invalid input format or missing required fields. Returns MCP JSON-RPC 2.0 error response. Common causes: Invalid JSON-RPC 2.0 format, missing required fields (jsonrpc, method/result/error, id), malformed params or result objects.Jz\n\003401\022s\nqUnauthorized - Missing or invalid API key. Ensure X-Cisco-AI-Defense-API-Key header is provided with a valid key.J\315\001\n\003403\022\305\001\n\302\001Forbidden - API key is valid but lacks permission for this operation. Possible reasons: Tenant does not have MCP inspection enabled, API key does not have access to the specified MCP connection.Jj\n\003429\022c\naToo Many Requests - Rate limit exceeded. Check X-Rate-Limit-Remaining header for available quota.J\235\001\n\003500\022\225\001\n\222\001Internal Server Error - An unexpected error occurred during inspection. If this persists, contact support with the X-Request-ID from the response.J\247\001\n\003503\022\237\001\n\234\001Service Unavailable - The inspection service is temporarily unavailable. This may be due to maintenance or high load. Please retry with exponential backoff.\202\323\344\223\002\030\"\023/api/v1/inspect/mcp:\001*'
